## Evidence boundary

DOCS ONLY. Every example is NOT RUN. Source reading establishes declarations and derivation paths, not successful compilation, server startup, or interoperability.

The retained Jet baseline names dirty HEAD f119f2041adfd25b2810e813d21a71050cf94bb6. It is not the identity of an exercised current binary.

Nest documentation was retrieved on 2026-09-11. It is unversioned. Registry records independently pin Nest 12.0.1, Swagger 12.0.1, and GraphQL/Apollo integrations 14.0.0.

Earlier Nest 11.1.6 source remains historical evidence. No complete resolved installation or complete matched protocol fixture was retained.

The full examples below are authored assemblies. They are not verbatim captured applications. Uncaptured API details and secondary package pins remain unverified.

## Common application fixture

The fixture constructs one order value per accepted request. It returns only its public ID. It does not claim database persistence or exactly-once order creation.

The stock code uses a serializable input and an explicit String failure. The adapter must not publish StoredOrder or its internal_note field.

```jet
