```

This call returns the existing JobQueue family, not a Redis-specific queue lifecycle.

Both arguments are required and nonempty.

Invalid or unavailable store opening uses the existing queue error carrier; it does not fabricate a working handle.

The exact existing enqueue, claim, acknowledge, recover_expired, receipt, events and status calls in the complete fixture are unchanged.

D-DX-QUEUE1=A keeps SQLite as default, explicit provider selection, Prelude-owned leases/retries and at-least-once effects.

The store must satisfy the existing typed durable-store transaction contract or be rejected.

No implicit SQLite fallback, hidden duplicate enqueue or second receipt identity is allowed.

Authored Redis recovery remains unproved; approval of this API does not certify a nonconforming implementation.

Exact current native enqueue returns Result<JetJobQueueReceipt, JetServiceError> at JobQueueNative.rs:49-61; Core.jet:64 exports JobQueue and does not export a new queue-specific error.

ServiceError is the existing service carrier, not JobError payload data.

Core.jet:85 exports core.service.ServiceError.

This exact existing error type is preserved.

