## Existing law and independent gates

Keep the existing cache absence contract: stored false, 0, and empty text are values, not misses. Absence uses the existing optional-value convention. A remote transport error is not absence. Never normalize a value by truthiness. The author uses cache as a concept, not proof of a current core.cache namespace.

D-CACHENAME1=A keeps Cache<K,V> and its current method law. D-DX-QUERY1=A/#2473 keeps Query identity, refresh, mutation, rollback, targeted invalidation, and state ownership. Router cache states stay separate. This storage adapter must not add another Query state model, HTTP response cache, or durable mutation queue.

The proposed open(endpoint, namespace, value_type) binds the existing cache value codec to remote storage. It takes two Strings and a checked value type. get returns an optional decoded value inside an error result. set takes key, value, and an explicit Duration named ttl. remove acknowledges removal through the same error result.

The proposed open/set/get/remove spelling is an exact API candidate, not a claim that an existing namespace exports it. Reconcile it with the canonical cache lookup before approval. Bool, Int, and String use the same rule; these are not separate cache policies. No new grammar or invariant exception is proposed.

Fixture consistency is one Redis primary, no replica reads, and no local read-through copy. After remove is acknowledged, later reads on that primary return absence. TTL is 1000ms from successful storage. At or beyond expiry, reads return absence. Concurrent earlier reads may still observe the earlier value.

An outage must produce an explicit transport error and must not return a fabricated miss or successful write. A disconnected write has an unknown result until reconciled. Do not retry secretly. Cache data is expendable; losing it on restart is a miss, never loss of authoritative order data. This vote does not change those existing boundaries.

The candidate Redis 7.2.5 endpoint is only an authored comparison fixture. No Redis client, Keyv package, production topology, default provider, or disclosure permission is approved for Jet. Cache package installation and exact binding require separate owner gates. Current miss, TTL, and invalidation proof remains with #3087.

