## Shared failure and restart sequence

1. Start the receiver, then run both event processes. Each local file contains one record. Run the selected sender once per file. Expected per-file report is delivered=1, failed=0; the receiver contains both records without token.

2. Stop the receiver. Run both services again in a fresh fixture directory, then invoke the sender for each new file. Expected report is delivered=0, failed=1. Each service result remains order-41. No retry, fallback destination, or hidden queue is allowed.

3. Restart the receiver without changing its endpoint. Local input files still exist. An explicit rerun may deliver them; an earlier ambiguous timeout can cause duplicates. The fixture accepts this limitation and does not imply exactly-once telemetry.

4. Supply an input file above 4096 bytes or above two records. The sender must reject it before sending. An invalid JSON record is also an input error. These limits are explicit fixture requirements, not newly approved global logging defaults.

