The exact API choice is D-NEST-GRAPHQL-API1.

This placement choice does not approve it.

Dependency disposition: neither option adds a Jet-linked third-party library, SDK, background broker, package installer, production endpoint or automatic download.

A is a first-party binding using existing runtime IO and the explicit protocol contract.

External broker servers are caller-selected services, never a stock default.

B leaves the complete peer adapter outside Jet.

Peer npm packages and versions are comparator fixture inputs only.

This is an explicit no-adoption boundary, not permission to choose an unnamed dependency later.

Any implementation that needs a new third-party dependency is outside this approved candidate contract.

Placement applies only if D-NEST-GRAPHQL-API1 selects A. If it selects B, the complete external adapter remains the final route and no Jet placement is needed.

## Recommendation reasoning and contract notes

A lets an application select the GraphQL bridge for this job without putting it in every CoreLib install. The same proposed workload and outcomes remain visible.

Option B: B makes every CoreLib installation carry GraphQL-specific code and release obligations, even when this job does not use it.

Option C: C makes each application recreate the GraphQL compatibility and security work for the same job.

Contract note: A requires explicit package selection and shared GraphQL compatibility work, while avoiding unused stock components.

