## Separate meaning and placement

This vote selects distribution and maintenance only. Each option uses the same proposed binding contract, inputs, protocol files, and caller outcomes.

The module names, package names, version 0.1.0, and bind functions below are explicit proposals. None is claimed to be a current Jet export.

No manifest schema is invented. A names a proposed first-party package. B names a proposed CoreLib module. C names an application module.

The imports use existing module-alias syntax. Exact package resolution and the new binding API need separate owner approval before implementation.

The peer package.json files configure Nest examples only. This vote selects no external Jet library, new command, production default, or remote disclosure.

The candidate bind consumes one checked App, validates the named public operations, and returns the same App with a protocol listener registration.

The existing App lifetime starts and stops that listener. A binding mismatch must reject before listening. There is no second application operation registry.

Binding and stream semantics remain owed under the separate semantic card. No placement can claim those semantics are already shipped.

D-DX-SERVERFN1=A and D-ENDPOINT-SHAPE1=A remain binding. Preserve typed public input, success, failure, capability, cancellation, and middleware facts.

Browser HTTP routes keep their same-origin policy. A non-browser protocol must not bypass capabilities or turn a transport status into successful application completion.

No new grammar, invariant exception, lifetime system, schema language, cloud service, or automatic publication is approved. No performance ranking is claimed.

## Exact GraphQL contract

GraphQL is a typed request protocol. This fixture has a required query root and one order mutation. The ready query reports only fixture availability.

Save this complete schema as orders.graphql. It is authored fixture data, not a captured generated schema.

```graphql
type Query { ready: Boolean! }
type Mutation { createOrder(sku: String!): String! }
```

The proposed bind maps mutation arguments by public field name to NewOrder. It maps the String success to createOrder without exposing StoredOrder.

The query ready maps to the checked data operation ready. It returns true. No implicit health endpoint or production readiness policy is approved.

The checked failure sku_required maps to a GraphQL error with message sku_required and extensions.code SKU_REQUIRED. The mutation result is non-null.

For the shown empty-sku mutation, the response has data:null and one error. Its path is ["createOrder"] and its location is line 1, column 12.

