## Exact proposed adapter contract

Socket.IO is an event protocol above its transport. Its event acknowledgement is not a native WebSocket frame acknowledgement.

The proposed serve call projects record-order from one checked App. It listens on loopback, uses path /socket.io and namespace /, and accepts the order event.

The proposed transports argument selects WebSocket transport for this fixture. It still requires the Socket.IO handshake and event framing; raw WebSocket data is not interchangeable.

The checked input is orders.Order. acknowledgement result sends the checked successful String result to that event's acknowledgement callback once.

The call returns Unit !Err for terminal serve failure. Action failure must not become a successful recorded receipt; absent success acknowledgement leaves the client's completion unknown.

Disconnect cancels connection-owned work and releases its state. Cancellation cannot undo a ledger transaction that already committed.

The client disables automatic reconnection and retries. It explicitly reconnects after a successful acknowledgement and resends the same business identity.

The ledger primary key, not Socket.IO, prevents a repeated charge. A lost acknowledgement does not prove failure and does not justify automatic mutation replay.

The Nest-only /connections observer reports gateway connection and pending-work counts. It is fixture instrumentation, not a required Jet public endpoint or a new telemetry API.

Jet cleanup proof must use its existing connection/resource facts or scoped instrumentation. The retained evidence does not establish a callable Jet counter or cancellation binding for this adapter.

No native WebSocket API is replaced. This vote neither selects connection-recovery defaults nor approves a new retry, delivery or operation-state model.

