decisions.detail:
## Bound common fixture

All code is NOT RUN. Use an isolated working directory with no earlier jobs or invoice files. The only input is order-41. Its enqueue key is invoice-41. The handler writes invoice-41.txt with exactly invoice:order-41, without a newline. No invoice service, database table, or helper is implicit.

The current baseline uses bundled SQLite in .jet/state/jobs.db. Leave JET_JOB_QUEUE_DB unset. A, B, and C use an isolated Redis 7.2.5 server at redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0. The queue is invoices. The Redis volume belongs only to this fixture. Loopback has no credentials; this is not a production security recommendation.

The following is Redis configuration syntax, not a Jet manifest. Start that server separately from its isolated persistent directory. No server was started for this repair.

```conf
bind 127.0.0.1
port 6379
appendonly yes
appendfsync always
save ""
maxmemory 64mb
maxmemory-policy noeviction
```

Common invoice.jet, used by current and every Jet option:

```jet
use core.files as files
#Job(.Dev) fn Invoice(order: String) {
    _ :: files.write(Path.from("invoice-41.txt"), "invoice:{order}")
        ?? panic("invoice write failed")
}
```

## Current workload

These current files are a source-backed adaptation, not a runtime receipt. They perform the same durable invoice job through SQLite. They do not satisfy the requested Redis placement. No captured Jet-level remote provider binding is assumed.

