D-DX-QUEUE1=A/#2457 remains binding. The Prelude owns enqueue, lease, acknowledge, retry, dead-letter, wait, and status. SQLite at .jet/state/jobs.db remains the default. The explicit configured database provider remains available. #2799 consumes that lifecycle; #2919 retains the runtime obligation.

This is one additional broker-store adapter, not a second job policy or a BullMQ lifecycle inside Jet. It must implement the existing typed durable-store contract. Reject a Redis candidate that cannot do so. Do not weaken current database transactions to make this fixture pass.

At-least-once delivery can repeat handler effects. A crash after writing invoice-41.txt but before acknowledgement permits the same write again. This fixture rewrites identical bytes; it does not establish exactly-once external effects. Real invoice systems must enforce their own durable idempotency.

