## Exact proposed adapter contract

Kafka offsets are positions, not business receipts. This fixture publishes a keyed JSON event, not a request needing a reply topic.

The proposed consume call selects one existing checked App action. It decodes each value as orders.Order and passes that typed input to record-order.

The proposed named arguments have exact meanings: from_beginning selects the first available record only when the group has no committed offset. commit accepts after-success here.

For partition offset n, after-success commits n+1 only after the checked action returns Ok. A rejected action must not commit that record.

The call returns Unit !Err. A terminal connection or commit failure returns Err, never a fabricated successful offset completion.

Rebalances can revoke a partition while work is active. The adapter must preserve partition ownership and expose uncertain completion through existing operation facts.

A consumer may see the record again after reconnect. This fixture's SQLite primary key prevents a repeated charge row; Kafka does not provide that business guarantee.

The scope does not set automatic retry, timeout, heartbeat, backpressure or rebalance defaults. A binding ballot must reconcile those details with existing checked operation law.

The retained Nest commit example passes the current offset unchanged. This authored workload deliberately commits the next offset, as the original assigned ballot already specified.

